      "factual_description": "National Sawdust presents Sensorium World on Thursday, November 19, 2026, centered on Paola Prestini and Brenda Shaughnessy’s Sensorium Ex, developed and produced by VisionIntoArt and Beth Morrison Projects. The current National Sawdust event page explicitly lists doors at 6:30 PM while also displaying 6:30 PM as the event time; because the primary source does not resolve whether that second field is the actual performance start, no showtime is inferred. The current page names Hailey McAvoy as Mem, Jakob Jordan as Kitsune and Jeffrey Zeigler on cello; it also credits Prestini for music, Shaughnessy for libretto, Jay Scheib and Jerron Herman for direction, Elizabeth Askren for music direction, Beth Morrison and Ras Dia for creative producing, and Luke DuBois as Sensorium AI software designer and project director. Sensorium AI uses vocal sampling of the performer’s own vocalizations to synthesize an expressive operatic voice, with depth-sensing gesture allowing the performer to manipulate pitch, pace and emotion in real time. VisionIntoArt identifies Sensorium Ex as an active project and records its world premiere as May 22–25, 2025 at the Common Senses Festival in Omaha, so this November 2026 National Sawdust performance is not described as a premiere.",
